 # Voxel Placement in Octree
 
-Also called: SVO set, Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) insertion with collapse/expand, octree voxel placement, placeVoxel
+Also called: SVO set, Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) insertion with collapse/expand, octree voxel placement, placeVoxel [S1, unofficial]
 
 ## Overview
-Voxel Placement in Octree is the fundamental recursive operation that inserts a colored voxel into a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) at a specific 3D coordinate, handling tree depth limits and node expansion [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of dynamically maintaining a hierarchical spatial index where internal nodes may be collapsed (merged into uniform leaves) and must be correctly expanded before further descent [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from its siblings: [Octree Insertion with Growth](2387-octree-insertion-with-growth.md) provides the broader context of boundary handling and tree growth, while [Dynamic Sparse Voxel Octree with Morton Codes](4099-dynamic-sparse-voxel-octree-with-morton-codes.md) focuses on linearization and cache efficiency rather than the raw recursive insertion logic [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Voxel Placement in Octree inserts a colored voxel into a Sparse Voxel Octree at a specific 3D coordinate, handling tree depth limits and node expansion [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of dynamically maintaining a hierarchical spatial index where internal nodes may be collapsed and must be correctly expanded before further descent [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Octree Insertion with Growth](2387-octree-insertion-with-growth.md) for boundary handling and tree growth, and differs from [Dynamic Sparse Voxel Octree with Morton Codes](4099-dynamic-sparse-voxel-octree-with-morton-codes.md) by focusing on raw recursive insertion logic rather than spatial linearization [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:**
-*   `node`: The current octree node (internal or leaf).
-*   `nx, ny, nz`: The world coordinates of the current node's center or origin (depending on implementation convention; S1 uses node center/origin for comparison).
-*   `size`: The side length of the current node's bounding box.
-*   `depth`: The current depth in the octree (0 is root).
-*   `x, y, z`: The target world coordinates of the voxel to insert.
-*   `color`: The color/value of the voxel.
-*   `maxDepth`: The maximum allowed depth of the octree.
